Figure 4 visually demonstrates that Nano-11 nanoparticles enhance antigen uptake by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Confocal microscopy images show efficient internalization of Nano-11 (red) by BMDCs. While soluble ovalbumin (OVA) alone (green) exhibits minimal cellular uptake, when OVA is adsorbed to Nano-11, both red and green signals are strongly present and co-localized within the BMDCs. This indicates that Nano-11 acts as an effective delivery vehicle, significantly increasing the intracellular amount of associated protein antigens.